  "id": "Compound::DB00717 - Gene::5243",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Norethindrone and Abcb1 through a series of molecular interactions involving estrone. Norethindrone is linked to the development of retinal vascular thrombosis and dermatitis hemorrhagic, both of which are associated with estrone. Estrone binds to Abcb1, indicating a possible role in the cellular uptake or transport of substrates. The lowest common ancestor in all three paths is the 3-hydroxy steroid, suggesting a shared pathway involving steroid metabolism. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in the connection between Norethindrone and Abcb1, though the specific mechanisms by which estrone mediates this interaction remain to be fully elucidated. The evidence is consistent across different disease outcomes, but the exact functional role of estrone in the binding to Abcb1 requires further investigation.",
